    "description": "Given an integer array nums, return all the triplets [nums[i], nums[j], nums[k]] such that i != j, i != k, and j != k, and nums[i] + nums[j] + nums[k] == 0.\nNotice that the solution set must not contain duplicate triplets.\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>3 &lt;= nums.length &lt;= 3000</li><li>-105 &lt;= nums[i] &lt;= 105</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> nums = [-1,0,1,2,-1,-4]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> [[-1,-1,2],[-1,0,1]]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> \nnums[0] + nums[1] + nums[2] = (-1) + 0 + 1 = 0.\nnums[1] + nums[2] + nums[4] = 0 + 1 + (-1) = 0.\nnums[0] + nums[3] + nums[4] = (-1) + 2 + (-1) = 0.\nThe distinct triplets are [-1,0,1] and [-1,-1,2].\nNotice that the order of the output and the order of the triplets does not matter.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> nums = [0,1,1]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> []\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> The only possible triplet does not sum up to 0.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 3</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> nums = [0,0,0]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> [[0,0,0]]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> The only possible triplet sums up to 0.</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
