    "description": "You are given the root of a binary tree containing digits from 0 to 9 only.\nEach root-to-leaf path in the tree represents a number.\nReturn the total sum of all root-to-leaf numbers. Test cases are generated so that the answer will fit in a 32-bit integer.\nA leaf node is a node with no children.\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>The number of nodes in the tree is in the range [1, 1000].</li><li>0 &lt;= Node.val &lt;= 9</li><li>The depth of the tree will not exceed 10.</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> root = [1,2,3]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 25\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span>\nThe root-to-leaf path 1->2 represents the number 12.\nThe root-to-leaf path 1->3 represents the number 13.\nTherefore, sum = 12 + 13 = 25.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> root = [4,9,0,5,1]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 1026\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span>\nThe root-to-leaf path 4->9->5 represents the number 495.\nThe root-to-leaf path 4->9->1 represents the number 491.\nThe root-to-leaf path 4->0 represents the number 40.\nTherefore, sum = 495 + 491 + 40 = 1026.</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
