    "description": "You are given an integer array nums and two integers indexDiff and valueDiff.\nFind a pair of indices (i, j) such that:\nReturn true if such pair exists or false otherwise.\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>2 &lt;= nums.length &lt;= 105</li><li>-109 &lt;= nums[i] &lt;= 109</li><li>1 &lt;= indexDiff &lt;= nums.length</li><li>0 &lt;= valueDiff &lt;= 109</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> nums = [1,2,3,1], indexDiff = 3, valueDiff = 0\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> true\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> We can choose (i, j) = (0, 3).\nWe satisfy the three conditions:\ni != j --> 0 != 3\nabs(i - j) <= indexDiff --> abs(0 - 3) <= 3\nabs(nums[i] - nums[j]) <= valueDiff --> abs(1 - 1) <= 0</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> nums = [1,5,9,1,5,9], indexDiff = 2, valueDiff = 3\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> false\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> After trying all the possible pairs (i, j), we cannot satisfy the three conditions, so we return false.</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
