    "companies": [
      "Google",
      "Microsoft",
      "Uber"
    ],
    "description": "You are given an integer array nums of length n.\nAssume arrk to be an array obtained by rotating nums by k positions clock-wise. We define the rotation function F on nums as follow:\nReturn the maximum value of F(0), F(1), ..., F(n-1).\nThe test cases are generated so that the answer fits in a 32-bit integer.\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>n == nums.length</li><li>1 &lt;= n &lt;= 105</li><li>-100 &lt;= nums[i] &lt;= 100</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> nums = [4,3,2,6]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 26\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span>\nF(0) = (0 * 4) + (1 * 3) + (2 * 2) + (3 * 6) = 0 + 3 + 4 + 18 = 25\nF(1) = (0 * 6) + (1 * 4) + (2 * 3) + (3 * 2) = 0 + 4 + 6 + 6 = 16\nF(2) = (0 * 2) + (1 * 6) + (2 * 4) + (3 * 3) = 0 + 6 + 8 + 9 = 23\nF(3) = (0 * 3) + (1 * 2) + (2 * 6) + (3 * 4) = 0 + 2 + 12 + 12 = 26\nSo the maximum value of F(0), F(1), F(2), F(3) is F(3) = 26.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> nums = [100]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 0</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
