    "description": "The Hamming distance between two integers is the number of positions at which the corresponding bits are different.\nGiven two integers x and y, return the Hamming distance between them.\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>0 &lt;= x, y &lt;= 231 - 1</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> x = 1, y = 4\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 2\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span>\n1   (0 0 0 1)\n4   (0 1 0 0)\n       ↑   ↑\nThe above arrows point to positions where the corresponding bits are different.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> x = 3, y = 1\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 1</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
