    "description": "The Hamming distance between two integers is the number of positions at which the corresponding bits are different.\nGiven an integer array nums, return the sum of Hamming distances between all the pairs of the integers in nums.\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>1 &lt;= nums.length &lt;= 104</li><li>0 &lt;= nums[i] &lt;= 109</li><li>The answer for the given input will fit in a 32-bit integer.</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> nums = [4,14,2]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 6\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> In binary representation, the 4 is 0100, 14 is 1110, and 2 is 0010 (just\nshowing the four bits relevant in this case).\nThe answer will be:\nHammingDistance(4, 14) + HammingDistance(4, 2) + HammingDistance(14, 2) = 2 + 2 + 2 = 6.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> nums = [4,14,4]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 4</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
