    "description": "Suppose you have n integers labeled 1 through n. A permutation of those n integers perm (1-indexed) is considered a beautiful arrangement if for every i (1 <= i <= n), either of the following is true:\nGiven an integer n, return the number of the beautiful arrangements that you can construct.\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>1 &lt;= n &lt;= 15</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> n = 2\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 2\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> \nThe first beautiful arrangement is [1,2]:\n    - perm[1] = 1 is divisible by i = 1\n    - perm[2] = 2 is divisible by i = 2\nThe second beautiful arrangement is [2,1]:\n    - perm[1] = 2 is divisible by i = 1\n    - i = 2 is divisible by perm[2] = 1</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> n = 1\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 1</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
