    "description": "Given an array of integers nums and an integer k, return the number of unique k-diff pairs in the array.\nA k-diff pair is an integer pair (nums[i], nums[j]), where the following are true:\nNotice that |val| denotes the absolute value of val.\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>1 &lt;= nums.length &lt;= 104</li><li>-107 &lt;= nums[i] &lt;= 107</li><li>0 &lt;= k &lt;= 107</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> nums = [3,1,4,1,5], k = 2\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 2\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> There are two 2-diff pairs in the array, (1, 3) and (3, 5).\nAlthough we have two 1s in the input, we should only return the number of unique pairs.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> nums = [1,2,3,4,5], k = 1\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 4\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> There are four 1-diff pairs in the array, (1, 2), (2, 3), (3, 4) and (4, 5).</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 3</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> nums = [1,3,1,5,4], k = 0\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 1\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> There is one 0-diff pair in the array, (1, 1).</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
