    "companies": [
      "Meta"
    ],
    "description": "Given an integer array nums of 2n integers, group these integers into n pairs (a1, b1), (a2, b2), ..., (an, bn) such that the sum of min(ai, bi) for all i is maximized. Return the maximized sum.\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>1 &lt;= n &lt;= 104</li><li>nums.length == 2 * n</li><li>-104 &lt;= nums[i] &lt;= 104</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> nums = [1,4,3,2]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 4\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> All possible pairings (ignoring the ordering of elements) are:\n1. (1, 4), (2, 3) -> min(1, 4) + min(2, 3) = 1 + 2 = 3\n2. (1, 3), (2, 4) -> min(1, 3) + min(2, 4) = 1 + 2 = 3\n3. (1, 2), (3, 4) -> min(1, 2) + min(3, 4) = 1 + 3 = 4\nSo the maximum possible sum is 4.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> nums = [6,2,6,5,1,2]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 9\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> The optimal pairing is (2, 1), (2, 5), (6, 6). min(2, 1) + min(2, 5) + min(6, 6) = 1 + 2 + 6 = 9.</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
