    "description": "Given two integers left and right, return the count of numbers in the inclusive range [left, right] having a prime number of set bits in their binary representation.\nRecall that the number of set bits an integer has is the number of 1's present when written in binary.\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>1 &lt;= left &lt;= right &lt;= 106</li><li>0 &lt;= right - left &lt;= 104</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> left = 6, right = 10\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 4\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span>\n6  -> 110 (2 set bits, 2 is prime)\n7  -> 111 (3 set bits, 3 is prime)\n8  -> 1000 (1 set bit, 1 is not prime)\n9  -> 1001 (2 set bits, 2 is prime)\n10 -> 1010 (2 set bits, 2 is prime)\n4 numbers have a prime number of set bits.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> left = 10, right = 15\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 5\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span>\n10 -> 1010 (2 set bits, 2 is prime)\n11 -> 1011 (3 set bits, 3 is prime)\n12 -> 1100 (2 set bits, 2 is prime)\n13 -> 1101 (3 set bits, 3 is prime)\n14 -> 1110 (3 set bits, 3 is prime)\n15 -> 1111 (4 set bits, 4 is not prime)\n5 numbers have a prime number of set bits.</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
