    "description": "You are given an integer array arr of length n that represents a permutation of the integers in the range [0, n - 1].\nWe split arr into some number of chunks (i.e., partitions), and individually sort each chunk. After concatenating them, the result should equal the sorted array.\nReturn the largest number of chunks we can make to sort the array.\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>n == arr.length</li><li>1 &lt;= n &lt;= 10</li><li>0 &lt;= arr[i] &lt; n</li><li>All the elements of arr are unique.</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> arr = [4,3,2,1,0]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 1\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span>\nSplitting into two or more chunks will not return the required result.\nFor example, splitting into [4, 3], [2, 1, 0] will result in [3, 4, 0, 1, 2], which isn't sorted.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> arr = [1,0,2,3,4]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 4\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span>\nWe can split into two chunks, such as [1, 0], [2, 3, 4].\nHowever, splitting into [1, 0], [2], [3], [4] is the highest number of chunks possible.</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
