    "description": "Your car starts at position 0 and speed +1 on an infinite number line. Your car can go into negative positions. Your car drives automatically according to a sequence of instructions 'A' (accelerate) and 'R' (reverse):\nFor example, after commands \"AAR\", your car goes to positions 0 --> 1 --> 3 --> 3, and your speed goes to 1 --> 2 --> 4 --> -1.\nGiven a target position target, return the length of the shortest sequence of instructions to get there.\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>1 &lt;= target &lt;= 104</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> target = 3\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 2\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> \nThe shortest instruction sequence is \"AA\".\nYour position goes from 0 --> 1 --> 3.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> target = 6\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 5\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> \nThe shortest instruction sequence is \"AAARA\".\nYour position goes from 0 --> 1 --> 3 --> 7 --> 7 --> 6.</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
