    "description": "The complement of an integer is the integer you get when you flip all the 0's to 1's and all the 1's to 0's in its binary representation.\nGiven an integer n, return its complement.\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>0 &lt;= n &lt; 109</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> n = 5\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 2\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> 5 is \"101\" in binary, with complement \"010\" in binary, which is 2 in base-10.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> n = 7\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 0\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> 7 is \"111\" in binary, with complement \"000\" in binary, which is 0 in base-10.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 3</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> n = 10\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 5\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> 10 is \"1010\" in binary, with complement \"0101\" in binary, which is 5 in base-10.</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
