    "description": "Given the root of a binary tree, find the maximum value v for which there exist different nodes a and b where v = |a.val - b.val| and a is an ancestor of b.\nA node a is an ancestor of b if either: any child of a is equal to b or any child of a is an ancestor of b.\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>The number of nodes in the tree is in the range [2, 5000].</li><li>0 &lt;= Node.val &lt;= 105</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> root = [8,3,10,1,6,null,14,null,null,4,7,13]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 7\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> We have various ancestor-node differences, some of which are given below :\n|8 - 3| = 5\n|3 - 7| = 4\n|8 - 1| = 7\n|10 - 13| = 3\nAmong all possible differences, the maximum value of 7 is obtained by |8 - 1| = 7.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> root = [1,null,2,null,0,3]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 3</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
