    "companies": [
      "Microsoft",
      "Netflix"
    ],
    "description": "You are given two integer arrays nums1 and nums2. We write the integers of nums1 and nums2 (in the order they are given) on two separate horizontal lines.\nWe may draw connecting lines: a straight line connecting two numbers nums1[i] and nums2[j] such that:\nNote that a connecting line cannot intersect even at the endpoints (i.e., each number can only belong to one connecting line).\nReturn the maximum number of connecting lines we can draw in this way.\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>1 &lt;= nums1.length, nums2.length &lt;= 500</li><li>1 &lt;= nums1[i], nums2[j] &lt;= 2000</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> nums1 = [1,4,2], nums2 = [1,2,4]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 2\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> We can draw 2 uncrossed lines as in the diagram.\nWe cannot draw 3 uncrossed lines, because the line from nums1[1] = 4 to nums2[2] = 4 will intersect the line from nums1[2]=2 to nums2[1]=2.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> nums1 = [2,5,1,2,5], nums2 = [10,5,2,1,5,2]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 3</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 3</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> nums1 = [1,3,7,1,7,5], nums2 = [1,9,2,5,1]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 2</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
