    "description": "Given the root of a binary tree, split the binary tree into two subtrees by removing one edge such that the product of the sums of the subtrees is maximized.\nReturn the maximum product of the sums of the two subtrees. Since the answer may be too large, return it modulo 109 + 7.\nNote that you need to maximize the answer before taking the mod and not after taking it.\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>The number of nodes in the tree is in the range [2, 5 * 104].</li><li>1 &lt;= Node.val &lt;= 104</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> root = [1,2,3,4,5,6]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 110\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> Remove the red edge and get 2 binary trees with sum 11 and 10. Their product is 110 (11*10)</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> root = [1,null,2,3,4,null,null,5,6]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 90\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> Remove the red edge and get 2 binary trees with sum 15 and 6.Their product is 90 (15*6)</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
