    "description": "Given two integer arrays arr1 and arr2, and the integer d, return the distance value between the two arrays.\nThe distance value is defined as the number of elements arr1[i] such that there is not any element arr2[j] where |arr1[i]-arr2[j]| <= d.\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>1 &lt;= arr1.length, arr2.length &lt;= 500</li><li>-1000 &lt;= arr1[i], arr2[j] &lt;= 1000</li><li>0 &lt;= d &lt;= 100</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> arr1 = [4,5,8], arr2 = [10,9,1,8], d = 2\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 2\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> \nFor arr1[0]=4 we have: \n|4-10|=6 > d=2 \n|4-9|=5 > d=2 \n|4-1|=3 > d=2 \n|4-8|=4 > d=2 \nFor arr1[1]=5 we have: \n|5-10|=5 > d=2 \n|5-9|=4 > d=2 \n|5-1|=4 > d=2 \n|5-8|=3 > d=2\nFor arr1[2]=8 we have:\n|8-10|=2 <= d=2\n|8-9|=1 <= d=2\n|8-1|=7 > d=2\n|8-8|=0 <= d=2</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> arr1 = [1,4,2,3], arr2 = [-4,-3,6,10,20,30], d = 3\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 2</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 3</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> arr1 = [2,1,100,3], arr2 = [-5,-2,10,-3,7], d = 6\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 1</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
