    "description": "Given a binary string s and an integer k, return true if every binary code of length k is a substring of s. Otherwise, return false.\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>1 &lt;= s.length &lt;= 5 * 105</li><li>s[i] is either &#039;0&#039; or &#039;1&#039;.</li><li>1 &lt;= k &lt;= 20</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> s = \"00110110\", k = 2\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> true\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> The binary codes of length 2 are \"00\", \"01\", \"10\" and \"11\". They can be all found as substrings at indices 0, 1, 3 and 2 respectively.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> s = \"0110\", k = 1\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> true\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> The binary codes of length 1 are \"0\" and \"1\", it is clear that both exist as a substring.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 3</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> s = \"0110\", k = 2\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> false\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> The binary code \"00\" is of length 2 and does not exist in the array.</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
