    "description": "Given an array of integers nums, find the maximum length of a subarray where the product of all its elements is positive.\nA subarray of an array is a consecutive sequence of zero or more values taken out of that array.\nReturn the maximum length of a subarray with positive product.\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>1 &lt;= nums.length &lt;= 105</li><li>-109 &lt;= nums[i] &lt;= 109</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> nums = [1,-2,-3,4]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 4\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> The array nums already has a positive product of 24.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> nums = [0,1,-2,-3,-4]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 3\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> The longest subarray with positive product is [1,-2,-3] which has a product of 6.\nNotice that we cannot include 0 in the subarray since that'll make the product 0 which is not positive.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 3</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> nums = [-1,-2,-3,0,1]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 2\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> The longest subarray with positive product is [-1,-2] or [-2,-3].</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
