    "description": "You own a Goal Parser that can interpret a string command. The command consists of an alphabet of \"G\", \"()\" and/or \"(al)\" in some order. The Goal Parser will interpret \"G\" as the string \"G\", \"()\" as the string \"o\", and \"(al)\" as the string \"al\". The interpreted strings are then concatenated in the original order.\nGiven the string command, return the Goal Parser's interpretation of command.\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>1 &lt;= command.length &lt;= 100</li><li>command consists of &quot;G&quot;, &quot;()&quot;, and/or &quot;(al)&quot; in some order.</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> command = \"G()(al)\"\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> \"Goal\"\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> The Goal Parser interprets the command as follows:\nG -> G\n() -> o\n(al) -> al\nThe final concatenated result is \"Goal\".</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> command = \"G()()()()(al)\"\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> \"Gooooal\"</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 3</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> command = \"(al)G(al)()()G\"\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> \"alGalooG\"</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
