    "description": "You are given an array pairs, where pairs[i] = [xi, yi], and:\nLet ways be the number of rooted trees that satisfy the following conditions:\nTwo ways are considered to be different if there is at least one node that has different parents in both ways.\nReturn:\nA rooted tree is a tree that has a single root node, and all edges are oriented to be outgoing from the root.\nAn ancestor of a node is any node on the path from the root to that node (excluding the node itself). The root has no ancestors.\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>1 &lt;= pairs.length &lt;= 105</li><li>1 &lt;= xi &lt; yi &lt;= 500</li><li>The elements in pairs are unique.</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> pairs = [[1,2],[2,3]]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 1\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> There is exactly one valid rooted tree, which is shown in the above figure.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> pairs = [[1,2],[2,3],[1,3]]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 2\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> There are multiple valid rooted trees. Three of them are shown in the above figures.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 3</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> pairs = [[1,2],[2,3],[2,4],[1,5]]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 0\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> There are no valid rooted trees.</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
