    "description": "Given an alphanumeric string s, return the second largest numerical digit that appears in s, or -1 if it does not exist.\nAn alphanumeric string is a string consisting of lowercase English letters and digits.\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>1 &lt;= s.length &lt;= 500</li><li>s consists of only lowercase English letters and digits.</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> s = \"dfa12321afd\"\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 2\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> The digits that appear in s are [1, 2, 3]. The second largest digit is 2.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> s = \"abc1111\"\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> -1\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> The digits that appear in s are [1]. There is no second largest digit.</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
