    "description": "The min-product of an array is equal to the minimum value in the array multiplied by the array's sum.\nGiven an array of integers nums, return the maximum min-product of any non-empty subarray of nums. Since the answer may be large, return it modulo 109 + 7.\nNote that the min-product should be maximized before performing the modulo operation. Testcases are generated such that the maximum min-product without modulo will fit in a 64-bit signed integer.\nA subarray is a contiguous part of an array.\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>1 &lt;= nums.length &lt;= 105</li><li>1 &lt;= nums[i] &lt;= 107</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> nums = [1,2,3,2]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 14\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> The maximum min-product is achieved with the subarray [2,3,2] (minimum value is 2).\n2 * (2+3+2) = 2 * 7 = 14.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> nums = [2,3,3,1,2]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 18\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> The maximum min-product is achieved with the subarray [3,3] (minimum value is 3).\n3 * (3+3) = 3 * 6 = 18.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 3</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> nums = [3,1,5,6,4,2]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 60\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> The maximum min-product is achieved with the subarray [5,6,4] (minimum value is 4).\n4 * (5+6+4) = 4 * 15 = 60.</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
