    "description": "You are given two integer arrays nums1 and nums2. You are tasked to implement a data structure that supports queries of two types:\nImplement the FindSumPairs class:\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>1 &lt;= nums1.length &lt;= 1000</li><li>1 &lt;= nums2.length &lt;= 105</li><li>1 &lt;= nums1[i] &lt;= 109</li><li>1 &lt;= nums2[i] &lt;= 105</li><li>0 &lt;= index &lt; nums2.length</li><li>1 &lt;= val &lt;= 105</li><li>1 &lt;= tot &lt;= 109</li><li>At most 1000 calls are made to add and count each.</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\">Input\n[\"FindSumPairs\", \"count\", \"add\", \"count\", \"count\", \"add\", \"add\", \"count\"]\n[[[1, 1, 2, 2, 2, 3], [1, 4, 5, 2, 5, 4]], [7], [3, 2], [8], [4], [0, 1], [1, 1], [7]]\nOutput\n[null, 8, null, 2, 1, null, null, 11]\n\nExplanation\nFindSumPairs findSumPairs = new FindSumPairs([1, 1, 2, 2, 2, 3], [1, 4, 5, 2, 5, 4]);\nfindSumPairs.count(7);  // return 8; pairs (2,2), (3,2), (4,2), (2,4), (3,4), (4,4) make 2 + 5 and pairs (5,1), (5,5) make 3 + 4\nfindSumPairs.add(3, 2); // now nums2 = [1,4,5,4,5,4]\nfindSumPairs.count(8);  // return 2; pairs (5,2), (5,4) make 3 + 5\nfindSumPairs.count(4);  // return 1; pair (5,0) makes 3 + 1\nfindSumPairs.add(0, 1); // now nums2 = [2,4,5,4,5,4]\nfindSumPairs.add(1, 1); // now nums2 = [2,5,5,4,5,4]\nfindSumPairs.count(7);  // return 11; pairs (2,1), (2,2), (2,4), (3,1), (3,2), (3,4), (4,1), (4,2), (4,4) make 2 + 5 and pairs (5,3), (5,5) make 3 + 4</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
