    "description": "You are given an array of strings words (0-indexed).\nIn one operation, pick two distinct indices i and j, where words[i] is a non-empty string, and move any character from words[i] to any position in words[j].\nReturn true if you can make every string in words equal using any number of operations, and false otherwise.\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>1 &lt;= words.length &lt;= 100</li><li>1 &lt;= words[i].length &lt;= 100</li><li>words[i] consists of lowercase English letters.</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> words = [\"abc\",\"aabc\",\"bc\"]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> true\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> Move the first 'a' in words[1] to the front of words[2],\nto make words[1] = \"abc\" and words[2] = \"abc\".\nAll the strings are now equal to \"abc\", so return true.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> words = [\"ab\",\"a\"]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> false\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> It is impossible to make all the strings equal using the operation.</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
