    "description": "Given an integer array nums of length n, you want to create an array ans of length 2n where ans[i] == nums[i] and ans[i + n] == nums[i] for 0 <= i < n (0-indexed).\nSpecifically, ans is the concatenation of two nums arrays.\nReturn the array ans.\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>n == nums.length</li><li>1 &lt;= n &lt;= 1000</li><li>1 &lt;= nums[i] &lt;= 1000</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> nums = [1,2,1]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> [1,2,1,1,2,1]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> The array ans is formed as follows:\n- ans = [nums[0],nums[1],nums[2],nums[0],nums[1],nums[2]]\n- ans = [1,2,1,1,2,1]</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> nums = [1,3,2,1]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> [1,3,2,1,1,3,2,1]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> The array ans is formed as follows:\n- ans = [nums[0],nums[1],nums[2],nums[3],nums[0],nums[1],nums[2],nums[3]]\n- ans = [1,3,2,1,1,3,2,1]</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
