    "description": "Given a 0-indexed integer array nums, return the number of distinct quadruplets (a, b, c, d) such that:\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>4 &lt;= nums.length &lt;= 50</li><li>1 &lt;= nums[i] &lt;= 100</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> nums = [1,2,3,6]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 1\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> The only quadruplet that satisfies the requirement is (0, 1, 2, 3) because 1 + 2 + 3 == 6.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> nums = [3,3,6,4,5]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 0\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> There are no such quadruplets in [3,3,6,4,5].</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 3</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> nums = [1,1,1,3,5]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 4\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> The 4 quadruplets that satisfy the requirement are:\n- (0, 1, 2, 3): 1 + 1 + 1 == 3\n- (0, 1, 3, 4): 1 + 1 + 3 == 5\n- (0, 2, 3, 4): 1 + 1 + 3 == 5\n- (1, 2, 3, 4): 1 + 1 + 3 == 5</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
