    "description": "Given an array of strings words, return the first palindromic string in the array. If there is no such string, return an empty string \"\".\nA string is palindromic if it reads the same forward and backward.\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>1 &lt;= words.length &lt;= 100</li><li>1 &lt;= words[i].length &lt;= 100</li><li>words[i] consists only of lowercase English letters.</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> words = [\"abc\",\"car\",\"ada\",\"racecar\",\"cool\"]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> \"ada\"\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> The first string that is palindromic is \"ada\".\nNote that \"racecar\" is also palindromic, but it is not the first.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> words = [\"notapalindrome\",\"racecar\"]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> \"racecar\"\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> The first and only string that is palindromic is \"racecar\".</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 3</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> words = [\"def\",\"ghi\"]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> \"\"\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> There are no palindromic strings, so the empty string is returned.</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
