    "description": "Reversing an integer means to reverse all its digits.\nGiven an integer num, reverse num to get reversed1, then reverse reversed1 to get reversed2. Return true if reversed2 equals num. Otherwise return false.\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>0 &lt;= num &lt;= 106</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> num = 526\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> true\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> Reverse num to get 625, then reverse 625 to get 526, which equals num.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> num = 1800\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> false\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> Reverse num to get 81, then reverse 81 to get 18, which does not equal num.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 3</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> num = 0\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> true\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> Reverse num to get 0, then reverse 0 to get 0, which equals num.</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
