    "description": "Given a string s consisting of only the characters 'a' and 'b', return true if every 'a' appears before every 'b' in the string. Otherwise, return false.\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>1 &lt;= s.length &lt;= 100</li><li>s[i] is either &#039;a&#039; or &#039;b&#039;.</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> s = \"aaabbb\"\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> true\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span>\nThe 'a's are at indices 0, 1, and 2, while the 'b's are at indices 3, 4, and 5.\nHence, every 'a' appears before every 'b' and we return true.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> s = \"abab\"\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> false\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span>\nThere is an 'a' at index 2 and a 'b' at index 1.\nHence, not every 'a' appears before every 'b' and we return false.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 3</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> s = \"bbb\"\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> true\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span>\nThere are no 'a's, hence, every 'a' appears before every 'b' and we return true.</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
