    "description": "You are given a 0-indexed integer array nums of even length consisting of an equal number of positive and negative integers.\nYou should return the array of nums such that the the array follows the given conditions:\nReturn the modified array after rearranging the elements to satisfy the aforementioned conditions.\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>2 &lt;= nums.length &lt;= 2 * 105</li><li>nums.length is even</li><li>1 &lt;= |nums[i]| &lt;= 105</li><li>nums consists of equal number of positive and negative integers.</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> nums = [3,1,-2,-5,2,-4]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> [3,-2,1,-5,2,-4]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span>\nThe positive integers in nums are [3,1,2]. The negative integers are [-2,-5,-4].\nThe only possible way to rearrange them such that they satisfy all conditions is [3,-2,1,-5,2,-4].\nOther ways such as [1,-2,2,-5,3,-4], [3,1,2,-2,-5,-4], [-2,3,-5,1,-4,2] are incorrect because they do not satisfy one or more conditions.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> nums = [-1,1]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> [1,-1]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span>\n1 is the only positive integer and -1 the only negative integer in nums.\nSo nums is rearranged to [1,-1].</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
