    "description": "You are given an integer array matches where matches[i] = [winneri, loseri] indicates that the player winneri defeated player loseri in a match.\nReturn a list answer of size 2 where:\nThe values in the two lists should be returned in increasing order.\nNote:\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>1 &lt;= matches.length &lt;= 105</li><li>matches[i].length == 2</li><li>1 &lt;= winneri, loseri &lt;= 105</li><li>winneri != loseri</li><li>All matches[i] are unique.</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> matches = [[1,3],[2,3],[3,6],[5,6],[5,7],[4,5],[4,8],[4,9],[10,4],[10,9]]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> [[1,2,10],[4,5,7,8]]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span>\nPlayers 1, 2, and 10 have not lost any matches.\nPlayers 4, 5, 7, and 8 each have lost one match.\nPlayers 3, 6, and 9 each have lost two matches.\nThus, answer[0] = [1,2,10] and answer[1] = [4,5,7,8].</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> matches = [[2,3],[1,3],[5,4],[6,4]]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> [[1,2,5,6],[]]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span>\nPlayers 1, 2, 5, and 6 have not lost any matches.\nPlayers 3 and 4 each have lost two matches.\nThus, answer[0] = [1,2,5,6] and answer[1] = [].</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
