    "description": "You are given a 0-indexed integer array nums. In one step, remove all elements nums[i] where nums[i - 1] > nums[i] for all 0 < i < nums.length.\nReturn the number of steps performed until nums becomes a non-decreasing array.\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>1 &lt;= nums.length &lt;= 105</li><li>1 &lt;= nums[i] &lt;= 109</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> nums = [5,3,4,4,7,3,6,11,8,5,11]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 3\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> The following are the steps performed:\n- Step 1: [5,3,4,4,7,3,6,11,8,5,11] becomes [5,4,4,7,6,11,11]\n- Step 2: [5,4,4,7,6,11,11] becomes [5,4,7,11,11]\n- Step 3: [5,4,7,11,11] becomes [5,7,11,11]\n[5,7,11,11] is a non-decreasing array. Therefore, we return 3.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> nums = [4,5,7,7,13]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 0\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> nums is already a non-decreasing array. Therefore, we return 0.</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
