    "description": "We call a positive integer special if all of its digits are distinct.\nGiven a positive integer n, return the number of special integers that belong to the interval [1, n].\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>1 &lt;= n &lt;= 2 * 109</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> n = 20\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 19\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> All the integers from 1 to 20, except 11, are special. Thus, there are 19 special integers.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> n = 5\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 5\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> All the integers from 1 to 5 are special.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 3</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> n = 135\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 110\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> There are 110 integers from 1 to 135 that are special.\nSome of the integers that are not special are: 22, 114, and 131.</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
