    "companies": [
      "Microsoft",
      "Amazon",
      "Uber"
    ],
    "description": "You are given two 0-indexed binary strings s and target of the same length n. You can do the following operation on s any number of times:\nFor example, if s = \"0110\", you can choose i = 0 and j = 2, then simultaneously replace s[0] with (s[0] OR s[2] = 0 OR 1 = 1), and s[2] with (s[0] XOR s[2] = 0 XOR 1 = 1), so we will have s = \"1110\".\nReturn true if you can make the string s equal to target, or false otherwise.\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>n == s.length == target.length</li><li>2 &lt;= n &lt;= 105</li><li>s and target consist of only the digits 0 and 1.</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> s = \"1010\", target = \"0110\"\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> true\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> We can do the following operations:\n- Choose i = 2 and j = 0. We have now s = \"0010\".\n- Choose i = 2 and j = 1. We have now s = \"0110\".\nSince we can make s equal to target, we return true.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> s = \"11\", target = \"00\"\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> false\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> It is not possible to make s equal to target with any number of operations.</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
