    "description": "Initially, you have a bank account balance of 100 dollars.\nYou are given an integer purchaseAmount representing the amount you will spend on a purchase in dollars, in other words, its price.\nWhen making the purchase, first the purchaseAmount is rounded to the nearest multiple of 10. Let us call this value roundedAmount. Then, roundedAmount dollars are removed from your bank account.\nReturn an integer denoting your final bank account balance after this purchase.\nNotes:\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>0 &lt;= purchaseAmount &lt;= 100</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> purchaseAmount = 9\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 90\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span>\nThe nearest multiple of 10 to 9 is 10. So your account balance becomes 100 - 10 = 90.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> purchaseAmount = 15\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 80\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span>\nThe nearest multiple of 10 to 15 is 20. So your account balance becomes 100 - 20 = 80.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 3</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> purchaseAmount = 10\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 90\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span>\n10 is a multiple of 10 itself. So your account balance becomes 100 - 10 = 90.</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
