    "description": "You are given positive integers n and target.\nAn array nums is beautiful if it meets the following conditions:\nReturn the minimum possible sum that a beautiful array could have modulo 109 + 7.\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>1 &lt;= n &lt;= 109</li><li>1 &lt;= target &lt;= 109</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> n = 2, target = 3\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 4\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> We can see that nums = [1,3] is beautiful.\n- The array nums has length n = 2.\n- The array nums consists of pairwise distinct positive integers.\n- There doesn't exist two distinct indices, i and j, with nums[i] + nums[j] == 3.\nIt can be proven that 4 is the minimum possible sum that a beautiful array could have.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> n = 3, target = 3\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 8\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> We can see that nums = [1,3,4] is beautiful.\n- The array nums has length n = 3.\n- The array nums consists of pairwise distinct positive integers.\n- There doesn't exist two distinct indices, i and j, with nums[i] + nums[j] == 3.\nIt can be proven that 8 is the minimum possible sum that a beautiful array could have.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 3</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> n = 1, target = 1\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 1\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> We can see, that nums = [1] is beautiful.</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
