    "description": "You are given an integer array a of size 4 and another integer array b of size at least 4.\nYou need to choose 4 indices i0, i1, i2, and i3 from the array b such that i0 < i1 < i2 < i3. Your score will be equal to the value a[0] * b[i0] + a[1] * b[i1] + a[2] * b[i2] + a[3] * b[i3].\nReturn the maximum score you can achieve.\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>a.length == 4</li><li>4 &lt;= b.length &lt;= 105</li><li>-105 &lt;= a[i], b[i] &lt;= 105</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> a = [3,2,5,6], b = [2,-6,4,-5,-3,2,-7]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 26\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> We can choose the indices 0, 1, 2, and 5. The score will be 3 * 2 + 2 * (-6) + 5 * 4 + 6 * 2 = 26 .</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> a = [-1,4,5,-2], b = [-5,-1,-3,-2,-4]\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> -1\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span> We can choose the indices 0, 1, 3, and 4. The score will be (-1) * (-5) + 4 * (-1) + 5 * (-2) + (-2) * (-4) = -1 .</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
