    "description": "You are given two integers n and m that consist of the same number of digits.\nYou can perform the following operations any number of times:\nThe integer n must not be a prime number at any point, including its original value and after each operation.\nThe cost of a transformation is the sum of all values that n takes throughout the operations performed.\nReturn the minimum cost to transform n into m. If it is impossible, return -1.\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>1 &lt;= n, m &lt; 104</li><li>n and m consist of the same number of digits.</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> n = 10, m = 12\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 85\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span>\nWe perform the following operations:</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> n = 4, m = 8\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> -1\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span>\nIt is impossible to make n equal to m .</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 3</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> n = 6, m = 2\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> -1\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span>\nSince 2 is already a prime, we can't make n equal to m .</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
