    "description": "You are given an array of integers nums of size n and a positive integer threshold.\nThere is a graph consisting of n nodes with the ith node having a value of nums[i]. Two nodes i and j in the graph are connected via an undirected edge if lcm(nums[i], nums[j]) <= threshold.\nReturn the number of connected components in this graph.\nA connected component is a subgraph of a graph in which there exists a path between any two vertices, and no vertex of the subgraph shares an edge with a vertex outside of the subgraph.\nThe term lcm(a, b) denotes the least common multiple of a and b.\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>1 &lt;= nums.length &lt;= 105</li><li>1 &lt;= nums[i] &lt;= 109</li><li>All elements of nums are unique.</li><li>1 &lt;= threshold &lt;= 2 * 105</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> nums = [2,4,8,3,9], threshold = 5\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 4\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span>\n\n\nThe four connected components are (2, 4) , (3) , (8) , (9) .</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> nums = [2,4,8,3,9,12], threshold = 10\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 2\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span>\n\nThe two connected components are (2, 3, 4, 8, 9) , and (12) .</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
