    "description": "You are given an integer array nums and an integer k.\nYour task is to partition nums into k non-empty subarrays. For each subarray, compute the bitwise XOR of all its elements.\nReturn the minimum possible value of the maximum XOR among these k subarrays.\n<div class=\"constraints-wrapper\"><h3 class=\"constraint-header\">Constraints</h3><ul class=\"constraint-list\"><li>1 &lt;= nums.length &lt;= 250</li><li>1 &lt;= nums[i] &lt;= 109</li><li>1 &lt;= k &lt;= n</li></ul></div>\n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 1</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> nums = [1,2,3], k = 2\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 1\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span>\nThe optimal partition is [1] and [2, 3] .\nThe maximum XOR among the subarrays is 1, which is the minimum possible.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 2</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> nums = [2,3,3,2], k = 3\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 2\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span>\nThe optimal partition is [2] , [3, 3] , and [2] .\nThe maximum XOR among the subarrays is 2, which is the minimum possible.</div>\n            </div>\n          \n            <div class=\"example-wrapper\">\n              <h3 class=\"example-header\">Example 3</h3>\n              <div class=\"example-block\"><br/><span class=\"ex-label input\">Input</span> nums = [1,1,2,3,1], k = 2\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label output\">Output</span> 0\n<br/><span class=\"ex-label explain\">Explanation</span>\nThe optimal partition is [1, 1] and [2, 3, 1] .\nThe maximum XOR among the subarrays is 0, which is the minimum possible.</div>\n            </div>\n          ",
